# Cursor rules — MultiPingTUI
# Short, dense context. Full docs: CLAUDE.md (read it before non-trivial changes).

project: MultiPingTUI
language: Go 1.24
binary: mping
domain: Terminal TUI for multi-host network probing (ICMP / TCP / system ping)
framework: bubbletea v1.3.10 + lipgloss + bubbles

# Entry points
- main.go: CLI flags, mode selection, global flags (DebugMode, SkipDNS)
- tui.go: TUI model (Elm-style, tea.Model)
- tui_list.go: list rendering, filter/sort logic
- pingwrapper.go: factory selecting ICMP/TCP/System backend by scheme
- pwstats.go: state machine for per-host stats
- status_server.go: HTTP sidecar (read-mostly)

# Architecture boundaries (strict)
- UI handlers MUST go through m.repo (HostRepository interface), never m.ps directly.
- UI state (cursor, scroll, viewMode) ≠ domain state (PWStats.state, wrapper lifecycle). Don't mix.
- Filter/sort logic lives ONLY in getFilteredWrappers (tui_list.go) and tui_utils.go. Don't branch in render.
- Stats are read from statsCache via getCachedStats. Never compute stats in render code.
- New shared state needs its own mutex, named for the field it protects.

# Anti-patterns (forbidden)
- No mock libraries. Hand-rolled fakes satisfying interfaces.
- No table-driven golden snapshots in first pass; substring assertions on rendered output.
- No interfaces with one implementation.
- No global locks; per-field mutex only.
- No time.Sleep > 1s in tests. Force UpdateRate100ms in test models.
- No reading wrapper internals outside CalcStats/Stats methods.
- No new deps without a written justification in the commit.

# Conventions
- One runnable check per non-trivial logic. No test frameworks.
- Inline comments explain WHY, not what.
- Mark deliberate shortcuts with `# ponytail: <ceiling>, <upgrade path>`.
- One logical change per commit.

# Tests
go test -race -count=1 ./...     # must pass; ~4s

# Key files for TUI work
- tui.go (Update/View lifecycle)
- tui_list.go (render + filter cache)
- tui_components.go (Header/Footer/HostList models)
- tui_test.go (5 user-flow tests, harness pattern)
- lifecycle_regression_test.go (regression suite)

# Conventions specific to this codebase
- Initial filter is set in NewTUIModel; cycle via nextFilterMode() in tui_utils.go.
- HeaderModel.filterMode and hostList.filterMode must stay in sync (cycle handler does this).
- Update tick is 100ms by default; stats refresh is gated by m.header.updateRate (header-driven, not body-driven).
- Edit-mode (key e) honors MPING_EDITOR env, falls back to -edit-config subprocess.